{
  "chance": {
    "all_type_tests": "at most 12 x 0.05",
    "primary_family": "at most 3 x 0.05 = 0.15"
  },
  "limitations": [
    {
      "group": 1,
      "id": "G1-1",
      "source": "scope feature 17, Done when",
      "text": "known answers and dbt share one reading of the Jira fields"
    },
    {
      "group": 1,
      "id": "G1-2",
      "source": "scope feature 17, Done when",
      "text": "the gold queries were model drafted blind to the answers, Q01 as a teaching pass, with counts only feedback, and Q01's pattern shaped the rest"
    },
    {
      "group": 1,
      "id": "G1-3",
      "source": "scope feature 17, Done when",
      "text": "`model_int` is written in SQL, so the graph may lean relational."
    },
    {
      "group": 2,
      "id": "G2-1",
      "source": "spec 0014 AC-4, AC-6 and the reach table",
      "text": "n is 20, with 6 or 7 questions per type, so a test with fewer than 6 untied questions can never read `real`, and `did not detect a gap` is not `equal`"
    },
    {
      "group": 2,
      "id": "G2-2",
      "source": "spec 0014 AC-4 and AC-7",
      "text": "the family bound of AC-4 and the chance line of AC-7"
    },
    {
      "group": 2,
      "id": "G2-3",
      "source": "spec 0014 rationale, Context (the literature look back, no longer in docs/session-notes.md)",
      "text": "the known answer code, the gold queries and the agent come from one model family, a shared blind spot and not a bias between stores"
    },
    {
      "group": 2,
      "id": "G2-4",
      "source": "spec 0014 rationale, Context; spec 0013 References (BIRD execution accuracy)",
      "text": "the strict score is all or nothing and not comparable to published execution accuracy"
    },
    {
      "group": 2,
      "id": "G2-5",
      "source": "spec 0011 AC-24",
      "text": "query and run times are recorded but never compared or ranked, because both stores run untuned in Docker on one laptop on a small dataset (spec 0011 AC-24)"
    },
    {
      "group": 2,
      "id": "G2-6",
      "source": "spec 0013 Follow-up",
      "text": "every scored run got the reading note, and plain runs are a lower bound that still carried shape, unit and hop limit (spec 0013 Follow-up)."
    },
    {
      "group": 3,
      "id": "G3-1",
      "source": "eval/data-description.md, Negative time entries (the 70 entries); docs/session-notes.md, Ruled out (about 1.5%); the CLOV 12% is in no file read (spec 0014 Follow-up)",
      "text": "hours count positive entries only, 70 negative entries left out (about 1.5% of counted seconds, CLOV about 12%)"
    },
    {
      "group": 3,
      "id": "G3-2",
      "source": "docs/session-notes.md, Q03 zero and Q16 zero; spec 0014 AC-14",
      "text": "Q03 and Q16 are zero answers, shown both ways"
    },
    {
      "group": 3,
      "id": "G3-3",
      "source": "scope, feature 17 candidates; not confirmed from any file read (spec 0014 Follow-up)",
      "text": "Q08 is one hop"
    },
    {
      "group": 3,
      "id": "G3-4",
      "source": "spec 0012 AC-7",
      "text": "Q10 is scored through its sources, and was told to return entities, not pairs, in both stores"
    },
    {
      "group": 3,
      "id": "G3-5",
      "source": "spec 0008",
      "text": "categories are properties, not labels (spec 0008)"
    },
    {
      "group": 3,
      "id": "G3-6",
      "source": "spec 0012 AC-17, AC-18",
      "text": "Q11 mixes people and projects in one set, and the sources of an empty, zero or false answer are `[]` (spec 0012 AC-17, AC-18)"
    },
    {
      "group": 3,
      "id": "G3-7",
      "source": "spec 0011 Follow-up",
      "text": "the literal check misses small numbers (spec 0011 Follow-up)."
    },
    {
      "group": 4,
      "id": "G4-1",
      "source": "spec 0012 Follow-up",
      "text": "the reading note's definitions and the list of source kinds were given"
    },
    {
      "group": 4,
      "id": "G4-2",
      "source": "spec 0012 Follow-up",
      "text": "temperature, `top_p` and `top_k` were the provider default and thinking was adaptive at effort low"
    },
    {
      "group": 4,
      "id": "G4-3",
      "source": "spec 0012 Follow-up",
      "text": "a run's label follows spec 0011 AC-10 as amended"
    },
    {
      "group": 4,
      "id": "G4-4",
      "source": "spec 0012 Follow-up",
      "text": "cap hits, timeouts and `limit_hit` per limit are shown beside every headline"
    },
    {
      "group": 4,
      "id": "G4-5",
      "source": "spec 0012 Follow-up",
      "text": "the agent was given the answer shape and unit of each question"
    },
    {
      "group": 4,
      "id": "G4-6",
      "source": "spec 0012 Follow-up",
      "text": "the 400,000 token limit was chosen so the 15 call limit binds first"
    },
    {
      "group": 4,
      "id": "G4-7",
      "source": "spec 0012 Follow-up",
      "text": "and if a real bug is found in the agent when no agent version is left (the cap is three), the runs are reported as they are and the bug is named here."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-1",
      "source": "spec 0015 Consequences and Follow-up, 2026-11-13; `docs/session-notes.md`, \"How others do it\", 2026-11-13",
      "text": "From agent version 2 the agent was told the evidence layout of each scored question, which version 1 had to infer, so version 1 and version 2 source scores are not compared, and the move from version 1 to version 2 is reported as a format change (spec 0015 changes format only)."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-2",
      "source": "spec 0015 Consequences, 2026-11-13",
      "text": "Noted runs can get a layout send back that plain runs cannot, because plain has no layout line; send backs appear in the log lines and are not recorded in run files."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-3",
      "source": "spec 0015 Consequences and Follow-up, 2026-11-13",
      "text": "Change C4 applies to Q09 only, with identical text in both stores; version 1 and version 2 Q09 counts are shown on their own line."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-4",
      "source": "spec 0015 Consequences and Follow-up, 2026-11-13",
      "text": "The layout check is soft, so a layout miss shows as `source_match` false and never as a lost answer by the layout alone; a send back can still lead the model into a structural slip, so the `no_answer` count of each version is printed (AC-33); a send back also spends model requests, so a run can end as `limit_hit` because of the layout check, and the `limit_hit` count of each version is printed beside it."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-5",
      "source": "spec 0015 Consequences, 2026-11-13, added after its review",
      "text": "Two sentences of the shared Sources text, \"Each kind may point at its own result.\" and \"A source column holds no NULL, so query a kind separately when some rows lack it.\", tell the agent how to shape its result tables, with identical text for every question and both stores; spec 0015 says they edge toward method."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-6",
      "source": "spec 0013 Consequences, 2026-11-11, and its Follow-up (undated); spec 0015 `index.md` line 100, 2026-11-13",
      "text": "The shared instruction text still speaks of a reading note in plain runs, in both stores, so the plain series is called \"without the reading note\", never \"cold\"."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-7",
      "source": "`docs/session-notes.md`, Q03 zero, 2026-11-11",
      "text": "Q03 is a zero answer with empty evidence, not a real zero, so a query that finds nothing scores correct and the zero says nothing about lateness; the stage reading is in the note."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-8",
      "source": "`docs/session-notes.md`, Q13 limitation, 2026-11-12",
      "text": "Q13 is scored as which sub-tasks of one issue (shape set, frozen); the score checks the sub-task IDs and, in the sources, every positive time entry on them, and does not check the summed hours, the assignee or the status."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-9",
      "source": "`docs/session-notes.md`, Q16 zero, 2026-11-13",
      "text": "Q16 is a real zero but a weak test: part of its filter never removes anything, so a query that gets that part wrong still scores correct; the stage reading is in the note."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-10",
      "source": "`docs/OrgOS-carry-forward.md`, \"Findings report (feature 17), additions\", file dated 2026-11-03",
      "text": "`eval/data-description.md`, already published, holds real looking names and emails taken from changelog display strings of the public CC BY 4.0 dataset, and `tests/fixtures/corpus/` possibly does too (not checked); they are not newly exposed and the file is not edited."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-11",
      "source": "`docs/OrgOS-carry-forward.md`, that section and its date; this spec's Consequences, 2026-11-11",
      "text": "The accuracy numbers hold only for this dataset, one model family and one load."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-12",
      "source": "the `time` field of the run files, the git tag `rule-frozen`, checked 2026-11-14",
      "text": "The commit tagged `rule-frozen` is dated 2026-11-11 at 23:57 UTC. The six version 1 Q01 runs (2026-11-11, 16:46 to 17:02 UTC) came before it; every other agent run came after it (version 1 from 2026-11-12, version 2 from 2026-11-13, the plain series from 2026-11-14). Replay files are not agent results."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-13",
      "source": "this amendment, 2026-11-14; spec 0015 commit `20d2486`, 2026-11-13 20:59 UTC",
      "text": "The measure of the version 1 against version 2 block (`answer_match`, Q09 apart) and the `no_answer` cells were set on 2026-11-14, after the version 1, version 2 and plain results had been seen; the measure follows spec 0015 line 165, written before the first version 2 run. The first form of AC-17 (a disagreement line) was replaced on 2026-11-14, also after the results were seen, by side by side counts, justified only by the cross check's list of decisions the disagreement rule needed."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-14",
      "source": "spec 0015 `rationale.md` \"How others do it\" (SWE-bench row), 2026-11-13",
      "text": "The layout line reveals the structure of the evidence grading, which is the kinds and the step count, never IDs."
    },
    {
      "group": 5,
      "id": "G5-15",
      "source": "spec 0015 `rationale.md` \"How others do it\", last row, 2026-11-13",
      "text": "The layout line is new: no benchmark read tells the model which record kinds to cite per question."
    }
  ],
